# This repository already ignores every *.log (root .gitignore:67), so nothing
# under logs/ is tracked. The rules below are therefore not what keeps the big
# logs out today — they are a standing refusal, so that a later `git add -f`
# cannot quietly pull them in.
#
# Why they must never be forced in: each *-deploy.log carries a literal
# `[info] Secret: <value>` line — the install pipeline still prints a credential
# in plaintext (the Stream-75 finding; reproduced on all four boxes on
# 2026-07-29). The same files also hold a few thousand long opaque strings per
# box (mostly image digests) that were not individually cleared.
#
# The logs stay on disk under logs/ as this run's evidence; the decisive lines
# are quoted in the report instead.
logs/*-deploy.log
logs/*-deliver.log
